UID:10011178-1786462200-1786473000@njaudubon.org
SUMMARY:Beach Birds of Summer
DESCRIPTION:Join CMBO Program Coordinator Adehl Schwaderer and CMBO Naturalists to search the Stone Harbor Point beaches for gulls\, terns\, and shorebirds! In summer\, Cape May County beaches attract an interesting range of terns\, gulls\, and shorebirds\, and this Special Field Trip offers a golden opportunity the subtle beauty of these birds. Common\, Forster’s and Least Terns are plentiful at this time\, and the Point is home to a successful colony of Black Skimmers. The group will walk the length of Stone Harbor Point and back\, taking their time to enjoy the cadre of common species\, separating shorebird species\, migrant and resident\, and so much more! We may walk up to 3 miles\, over sandy terrain. \nPREREGISTRATION REQUIRED – Ticket sales end 24hrs before the event \n\n\nCOST: $20 members\, $25 nonmembers. \nInterested in becoming a member? Please click on the following link to learn more or join: Become a Member today! \nIMPORTANT INFORMATION: \n\n\nWe bird in all weather. Be sure to check the forecast in advance and dress in layers appropriate for prevailing weather conditions. The weather in Cape May can differ considerably from nearby inland areas and may be warmer\, colder\, or windier so it’s best to be over prepared. We may have to bird in the rain\, so please bring your rain gear. \n\n\n\nTRANSPORTATION: Please arrive at the appointed time with a full tank of gas\, as transportation to field sites is by private vehicles. We may walk up to 3 miles\, over sandy terrain. \nCANCELLATION: CMBO programs require a minimum number of registrants to run\, five days in advance of the start of the tour but are seldom cancelled. If we do cancel\, due to lack of participation\, severe weather\, or unforeseen circumstances\, we notify all participants in advance\, and all are eligible for a full credit or refund. Participants may cancel without penalty if greater than 30 days in advance. Cancellations 10 to 30 days in advance may be subject to a 25% service charge. No refunds or credits for cancellations less than ten days in advance unless due to health emergencies \n\n\nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/beach-birds-of-summer-4/
LOCATION:Stone Harbor Point – 2nd Ave Parking Lot\, NJ\, United States
CATEGORIES:Bird Walk,Birding,Cape May Bird Observatory,Cape May Bird Observatory's Northwood Center,Field Trip
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/BeachBirdsOfSummer_Eventbright_2160x1080.jpg
GEO:39.035154182676;-74.770926744765
